Three encoders (125M--355M) differ in pretraining; same-architecture scaling is needed. Mean pooling matches BiGRU and shuffling produces $|\Delta| < 1$\,pp (Section~\ref{sec:decomposition}), confirming order-invariant detection. CKA confirms DAPT reshapes representations non-monotonically (Appendix~\ref{sec:cka_heatmap}). TF-IDF collapse on ActorAttack (0.261 vs.\ 0.961 on DD) demonstrates beyond-lexical features (Section~\ref{sec:limitations}).

